      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Religious conservatives argue that medical aid in dying, or euthanasia, is fundamentally immoral because it violates the sanctity of life, which is a divine gift. They believe that only God has the authority to end life, and human intervention in this process is a form of playing God and undermines the inherent value of human life. On the other hand, religious liberals tend to emphasize compassion, autonomy, and the alleviation of suffering. They argue that individuals should have the right to choose a dignified death when faced with unbearable pain and suffering, and that this choice aligns with the principles of mercy and compassion found in many religious teachings.",
